WEBVTT

00:05.150 --> 00:06.900
It appears that I survived, huh?

00:18.570 --> 00:21.120
Because... you're still alive.

00:21.730 --> 00:23.200
Please...

00:28.870 --> 00:30.340
Ah! It's hot!

00:35.230 --> 00:37.570
Please... give me a reward.

00:39.870 --> 00:41.520
The second movement?

00:43.650 --> 00:46.670
Love, I've got to feel it

00:46.950 --> 00:50.000
If you put your trust in me

00:50.270 --> 00:53.520
I know what my life would be

00:53.590 --> 00:58.410
Oh, you are all I ever need

00:58.570 --> 01:04.110
I try to hear what you say

01:04.260 --> 01:06.380
So I pray

01:06.460 --> 01:09.960
But you're fading away

01:11.400 --> 01:17.120
Don't go and break my fragile heart

01:17.550 --> 01:20.750
We won't fall apart

01:20.870 --> 01:28.930
'Cause you're my only star

01:30.890 --> 01:34.640
I wonder why my tears come at night

01:34.640 --> 01:38.150
Calling you, so like a little child

01:38.310 --> 01:41.390
All the things you have in mind

01:41.650 --> 01:44.770
I wish I could see your insides

01:44.770 --> 01:47.800
My love, you've got to feel it

01:47.800 --> 01:51.110
And if we put our trust in you and me

01:51.320 --> 01:54.770
You know what our lives would be

01:54.890 --> 02:02.730
Oh, you are the one, I believe

02:30.210 --> 02:32.170
Damn it!

02:32.170 --> 02:34.670
It can't be helped. I'm going to have to use my last resort.

02:34.670 --> 02:35.170
Sent History

02:34.670 --> 02:35.170
Miyako

02:34.670 --> 02:35.170
Kei

02:34.670 --> 02:35.170
Kyousuke

02:34.670 --> 02:35.170
Nagi

02:35.170 --> 02:36.670
Compose New Message

02:35.170 --> 02:36.670
Hirono Nagi

02:35.170 --> 02:36.670
Sorry, I need your help

02:35.170 --> 02:36.670
Hiro

02:36.670 --> 02:38.670
embrace

02:40.430 --> 02:41.760
Why...

02:42.680 --> 02:46.020
Why is it that everyone dies?

02:47.270 --> 02:48.020
A cold?

02:48.020 --> 02:49.100
Yeah.

02:49.100 --> 02:51.440
Mizuki's been a bit feverish since this morning.

02:51.440 --> 02:52.400
I see.

02:52.900 --> 02:55.070
Here's some soft-serve ice cream.

02:55.400 --> 02:58.610
It was supposed to be a present, but now it's a get-well gift, okay?

02:58.610 --> 03:00.650
There's some for everyone, so please eat it right up.

03:00.650 --> 03:02.070
Thank you very much.

03:02.070 --> 03:03.740
How's Mizuki-chan doing?

03:04.160 --> 03:08.000
She's just feeling a bit ill. Everything else seems fine.

03:08.000 --> 03:10.250
She's taken some medicine and is sleeping right now.

03:10.250 --> 03:11.370
I see.

03:11.370 --> 03:14.460
Well, I'll just go peek at her sleeping face and leave for today.

03:26.010 --> 03:27.890
Sorry about the other night.

03:27.890 --> 03:29.390
Rest well today.

03:33.980 --> 03:35.110
...lp.

03:37.570 --> 03:38.530
Mizuki-chan?

03:51.410 --> 03:53.830
He... lp.

03:57.250 --> 04:00.260
Good morning, Princess.

04:00.260 --> 04:02.010
Kuze... san?

04:02.510 --> 04:03.590
Are you all right?

04:04.340 --> 04:07.260
Yes. As long as an angel keeps smiling at me.

04:15.310 --> 04:17.110
Renji will see us.

04:17.110 --> 04:19.570
This is just mouth-to-mouth resuscitation, so it's all right.

04:19.570 --> 04:20.900
Mouth-to-mouth resuscitation?

04:20.900 --> 04:21.490
Yes!

04:21.490 --> 04:25.990
Yesterday's was a reward, and this one is mouth-to-mouth resuscitation!

04:25.990 --> 04:27.990
how

04:29.240 --> 04:31.700
Himura-senpai, sorry to make you wait!

04:31.700 --> 04:32.960
You're late.

04:32.960 --> 04:36.130
I'm so sorry. I overslept a bit.

04:36.130 --> 04:39.750
I couldn't really get to sleep, and I ended up falling asleep at dawn.

04:39.750 --> 04:41.260
Maybe I was nervous.

04:41.260 --> 04:43.630
A surprisingly cute characteristic of mine, don't you think?

04:43.630 --> 04:45.430
I get it. Let's go.

04:45.430 --> 04:48.550
I don't feel like wasting even more time on your outright nonsense.

04:48.550 --> 04:51.270
Okay! Well then, what should we eat for lunch?

04:52.100 --> 04:53.770
I thought we were going to buy you shoes!

04:53.770 --> 04:55.770
I didn't say anything about eating with you.

04:55.770 --> 04:59.150
Why do you think I decided to meet you at lunchtime?

04:59.400 --> 05:01.400
I don't eat lunch.

05:01.690 --> 05:03.150
I do, though!

05:05.860 --> 05:08.660
I've always wanted to come here.

05:08.660 --> 05:10.530
This place has a nice atmosphere, doesn't it?

05:10.580 --> 05:12.240
Oh. Okay.

05:12.240 --> 05:14.410
You don't have to be mad at me.

05:14.410 --> 05:15.960
It's not your kind of place?

05:15.960 --> 05:19.420
I'm not interested in eating out in the first place.

05:19.420 --> 05:23.090
Do you not eat lunch because...

05:23.090 --> 05:23.960
Yeah, it's because of money.

05:23.960 --> 05:25.470
I see.

05:25.470 --> 05:27.640
Well then, I'll pay the bill here—

05:27.640 --> 05:29.640
Don't do something unnecessary.

05:31.180 --> 05:33.720
It's not like I'm completely out of money.

05:33.720 --> 05:36.230
I'm just saving it for my tuition fees.

05:36.230 --> 05:37.100
Tuition fees?

05:37.100 --> 05:38.940
Are you going on to the next year?

05:38.940 --> 05:39.690
Yeah.

05:39.980 --> 05:43.320
'Cause everything burned down, and I've lost it all.

05:43.320 --> 05:46.900
I've hit rock bottom, so there's nothing for me to do but look up, is there?

05:47.240 --> 05:50.370
Himura-senpai, you're amazing, just as I thought.

05:50.370 --> 05:52.990
No matter what situation you're in, you don't give up.

05:52.990 --> 05:54.950
It's not like that.

05:54.950 --> 06:00.380
Because I don't have anything to protect, I can aim higher without thinking about the time I fell.

06:00.380 --> 06:02.460
And that's all there is to it.

06:02.460 --> 06:06.220
So you're just going to look up and not draw anymore?

06:06.220 --> 06:07.590
You!

06:07.590 --> 06:09.640
Did Amamiya send you or something?

06:09.640 --> 06:11.510
No, he didn't!

06:11.930 --> 06:15.770
No matter what anyone says,
I don't plan on drawing anymore.

06:15.770 --> 06:17.890
I told you, that wasn't my intention.

06:17.890 --> 06:21.900
It's just that I... really liked the pictures you used to draw.

06:21.900 --> 06:23.820
That was child's play.

06:23.820 --> 06:26.900
I can't make a living that way.

06:26.900 --> 06:28.200
Is that so?

06:28.200 --> 06:30.450
Well then, should we leave?

06:30.450 --> 06:31.870
What about your meal?

06:31.870 --> 06:33.740
I'm going to skip lunch as well.

06:33.740 --> 06:35.580
This and that have nothing to do with each other!

06:35.830 --> 06:39.710
I can't eat if you don't.

06:42.040 --> 06:44.210
Sheesh, what a waste of money.

06:45.880 --> 06:47.880
Love

06:48.090 --> 06:50.930
A new pair really feels great, right?

06:50.930 --> 06:53.930
You picked the same ones as last time, after all that thought?

06:56.390 --> 06:58.930
These are my favorites.

06:58.930 --> 07:00.730
But they're pretty cheap.

07:00.730 --> 07:04.020
Well, we can't be sure that they won't be damaged again.

07:06.070 --> 07:08.940
Are you sure you don't want me to punish those girls?

07:08.940 --> 07:12.360
If <i>you were to threaten them, it would end up as a permanent trauma!</i>

07:12.360 --> 07:15.080
Somehow, I feel like punishing <i>you now.</i>

07:15.080 --> 07:17.620
Eeeek!

07:17.620 --> 07:22.370
Senpai, you're finally going to bully me, aren't you?!

07:22.370 --> 07:25.340
Yuko, is this your way of living?

07:26.500 --> 07:29.340
Even if something unpleasant happens, you laugh it off.

07:29.340 --> 07:32.010
You fool yourself and act like it isn't painful.

07:32.590 --> 07:35.220
Is that really all right?

07:35.220 --> 07:37.890
It's all right, because I'm having fun right now.

07:37.890 --> 07:41.850
Also, because of what happened, I'm on a date with my admired senpai!

07:41.850 --> 07:43.810
You sure have a memorable way of living.

07:43.810 --> 07:45.310
Whoa, wait a second!

07:45.310 --> 07:46.860
This isn't a date!

07:46.860 --> 07:48.360
You're far too late,

07:48.360 --> 07:50.400
since I consider it a date.

07:50.400 --> 07:52.150
Hey, don't be selfish!

07:52.490 --> 07:56.160
Could it be that this is your first date as well?

07:57.490 --> 07:59.080
It <i>is your first, isn't it?</i>

07:59.830 --> 08:01.460
I didn't say anything.

08:01.460 --> 08:03.460
Yay, I'm so glad!

08:03.460 --> 08:04.460
Hey, wait!

08:04.750 --> 08:08.210
Since it's the first time for both of us, it will be an important anniversary, won't it?

08:09.510 --> 08:12.260
Say what you want.

08:12.260 --> 08:13.550
Himura-senpai?

08:13.550 --> 08:14.220
What is it?

08:14.220 --> 08:18.390
To tell you the truth, I want you to accompany me to one more place.

08:18.390 --> 08:20.390
it

08:21.600 --> 08:24.600
Wow, this really hasn't changed at all!

08:25.400 --> 08:29.730
Oh? Did I say something to annoy you again?

08:29.730 --> 08:32.190
You made me come back to a place like this.

08:32.190 --> 08:33.610
You can't blame me for being unhappy.

08:33.610 --> 08:36.160
As for me, I've always wanted to revisit this place.

08:38.830 --> 08:40.490
This is from the orphanage, isn't it?

08:40.490 --> 08:43.000
I'm sure they've been told not to play around here.

08:43.000 --> 08:46.420
Oh, so there are <i>still kids that don't listen to the teacher?</i>

08:46.420 --> 08:47.580
What are you trying to say?

08:47.580 --> 08:51.340
There was one kid who'd sneak out of there habitually, you know.

08:52.760 --> 08:57.680
And a certain other kid would habitually
sneak out with him and follow him around.

08:58.890 --> 09:01.390
Cute fugitives, don't you think?

09:01.390 --> 09:03.390
I

09:04.640 --> 09:06.520
This place hasn't changed much, either.

09:08.520 --> 09:09.480
Oh?

09:09.480 --> 09:10.270
Nii-san!

09:10.690 --> 09:12.610
Why are <i>you here, Amamiya-sensei?</i>

09:13.940 --> 09:17.990
I thought it was rather unusual for Yuko to go on an outing, but...

09:18.530 --> 09:19.490
I see.

09:19.490 --> 09:21.990
Sensei, are you sure you're not misunderstanding the situation?

09:21.990 --> 09:24.540
Being young is wonderful, isn't it?

09:24.540 --> 09:25.370
Whoa.

09:26.040 --> 09:27.710
Are you here to worship?

09:27.710 --> 09:31.500
I didn't know you were Christian, Amamiya-sensei.

09:31.500 --> 09:34.340
Nah, not me. My sister.

09:34.880 --> 09:35.920
Sister?

09:35.920 --> 09:37.180
Yuko, here.

09:39.430 --> 09:41.560
Oh, geez!

09:45.350 --> 09:49.770
Himura-kun, have you perhaps already performed illicit sexual activities with Yuko?

09:49.770 --> 09:51.270
Wh-What are you...

09:51.270 --> 09:53.480
Will you let me give you a piece of advice?

09:53.480 --> 09:55.030
I told you, I'm not...

09:55.030 --> 10:00.030
If you want to make Yuko yours, then prepare yourself.

10:00.450 --> 10:01.490
Prepare?

10:01.870 --> 10:06.410
If you lay a finger on Yuko without preparation, you'll definitely regret it.

10:06.830 --> 10:08.830
I don't have any such intentions.

10:11.290 --> 10:15.920
No matter what your intentions are, it seems like you've taken the first step.

10:16.800 --> 10:18.380
Geez...

10:18.380 --> 10:20.220
What did brother say?

10:20.220 --> 10:22.300
Just his usual jabber.

10:22.300 --> 10:25.720
But besides that, are you Christian?

10:25.720 --> 10:27.560
No, I'm not.

10:27.560 --> 10:30.400
But he said earlier that his sister was a believer.

10:30.400 --> 10:32.650
He wasn't talking about me.

10:32.650 --> 10:36.650
Nii-san is just like you, Himura-senpai.

10:36.650 --> 10:40.320
Nii-san lost his little sister in that earthquake.

10:41.320 --> 10:43.620
He... lost his sister as well?

10:45.830 --> 10:50.040
He's a very sad man as well.

10:50.040 --> 10:53.540
two hands, joining together

10:50.040 --> 10:53.540
After the time of encounter

10:57.050 --> 10:58.880
What's this, an ambush?

10:58.880 --> 11:01.550
"Ambush" isn't a very appealing word.

11:02.800 --> 11:05.640
We have the day off, so why are you in your uniform?

11:05.640 --> 11:08.060
I rarely wear regular clothing.

11:08.060 --> 11:09.890
You don't change at home either?

11:09.890 --> 11:11.020
Too much of a hassle.

11:11.020 --> 11:12.600
What about after you take your bath?

11:12.600 --> 11:15.360
I just go to sleep afterwards, so I don't wear anything.

11:15.360 --> 11:18.110
You have a younger brother at home, don't you?

11:18.110 --> 11:21.530
Yeah. I've got a younger brother, and my father is there too.

11:21.530 --> 11:22.910
They're both painters.

11:22.910 --> 11:24.740
This is precisely why artists are...

11:25.330 --> 11:28.750
Amamiya-sensei visited my house a little while ago.

11:29.120 --> 11:30.160
Amamiya?

11:30.580 --> 11:35.130
He was a student in my father's drawing class,
so he occasionally comes to visit,

11:35.130 --> 11:37.130
although he doesn't draw anymore.

11:37.130 --> 11:39.460
Even though he's an art teacher?

11:39.460 --> 11:40.670
Yeah.

11:40.670 --> 11:44.220
Ever since that earthquake, Amamiya-sensei hasn't drawn anything new.

11:46.310 --> 11:47.850
I see.

11:47.850 --> 11:50.020
He's a hardcore idiot as well.

11:51.140 --> 11:52.600
What's up, Nagi?

11:52.600 --> 11:54.480
Amamiya-sensei...

11:55.230 --> 11:58.730
He told me that he saw you and Yuko-chan on a date today,

11:58.730 --> 12:00.690
but is that true?

12:00.690 --> 12:04.450
I mean, you don't have to tell me about it, but can you blame me for being curious?

12:05.120 --> 12:09.750
And we're friends too, so I don't think
we should keep things from each other.

12:09.870 --> 12:13.000
I think you should tell me the real situation here.

12:13.000 --> 12:13.750
Hold on!

12:15.130 --> 12:17.460
Slow down a bit.

12:17.460 --> 12:19.630
Oh, sorry about that.

12:19.630 --> 12:21.800
It wasn't a date. We were just out shopping.

12:21.800 --> 12:24.470
It's exactly like the times when you drag me around.

12:24.470 --> 12:27.470
Anyway, why are <i>you worried about it?</i>

12:28.260 --> 12:30.930
It's not important, is it?

12:30.930 --> 12:33.100
I feel like I'm going to start hating you soon.

12:36.940 --> 12:38.360
What the hell?

12:38.360 --> 12:40.360
on

12:41.110 --> 12:45.320
At a time like this, which one do you think better represents the springtime of youth:

12:45.320 --> 12:47.160
me punching you, or you punching me?

12:47.160 --> 12:49.870
At a time like this, I really don't want to
experience the springtime of youth with you.

12:50.290 --> 12:52.750
You're the one who led Mizuki-chan on, aren't you?

12:52.750 --> 12:55.670
"Led" isn't the appropriate word.

12:55.670 --> 12:58.000
Still, I'm not mistaken that you encouraged her, right?

12:58.000 --> 13:00.550
She made the decision of her own accord.

13:00.550 --> 13:03.800
All I did was give her words of advice as a "helpful older man".

13:04.340 --> 13:07.550
Let's go. The results of your test should be ready.

13:11.010 --> 13:13.100
Which one should I draw next?

13:13.100 --> 13:14.940
You're done <i>already, aneki?</i>

13:14.940 --> 13:16.850
You're just slow.

13:17.350 --> 13:18.860
Should I draw this one?

13:18.860 --> 13:21.270
Nah, that one's fine. I'll draw the characters myself.

13:21.270 --> 13:22.990
Will you finish in time that way?

13:22.990 --> 13:24.280
It's integral to my pride.

13:24.280 --> 13:28.160
Those words should only come from someone who makes his deadlines.

13:30.330 --> 13:32.540
If you've got any complaints, then hurry up and draw!

13:32.540 --> 13:34.450
If not, <i>I'll draw everything.</i>

13:34.450 --> 13:36.620
I'll pay you an assistant's fee.

13:36.620 --> 13:37.620
I don't want it.

13:37.620 --> 13:39.710
I make a lot more than you do.

13:39.710 --> 13:42.380
I'll add your name to the "special thanks" list then, so...

13:42.380 --> 13:43.460
I don't want it.

13:43.460 --> 13:45.510
I'm merely imitating your bad form.

13:45.510 --> 13:48.930
I'd feel horrible if people viewed this as representative of my abilities.

13:48.930 --> 13:50.800
You're making <i>me feel horrible!</i>

13:50.800 --> 13:52.680
Whatever, just keep moving your hand.

13:52.680 --> 13:57.190
I have to go to Australia soon.

13:57.190 --> 14:02.400
Hiro, you quit school of your own accord
and decided to focus on being a mangaka

14:02.400 --> 14:05.190
without discussing it with me at all.

14:05.190 --> 14:06.400
My bad.

14:06.400 --> 14:09.110
Nah, you're not bad. I'm proud of your decision.

14:09.110 --> 14:10.070
Aneki?

14:10.070 --> 14:13.490
But now that you've decided, the responsibility is all yours.

14:13.490 --> 14:16.870
I'll help you out, but suffering is part of <i>your role.</i>

14:16.870 --> 14:18.170
Suffer to the max.

14:20.460 --> 14:22.710
Received

14:20.460 --> 14:22.710
Miyako

14:20.460 --> 14:22.710
Yoohoo~ ♪

14:20.460 --> 14:22.710
Is your script moving along?

14:20.460 --> 14:22.710
After you're done with work,

14:20.460 --> 14:22.710
let's go out and play!

14:24.590 --> 14:26.470
I guess it can't be helped.

14:26.470 --> 14:28.590
Yoohoo~

14:26.470 --> 14:28.590
Sorry, I've got my hands

14:26.470 --> 14:28.590
full at the moment, I'll

14:26.470 --> 14:28.590
contact you again later.

14:28.590 --> 14:31.010
The same reply again?

14:31.010 --> 14:32.600
How boring.

14:32.930 --> 14:34.430
Well then...

14:36.640 --> 14:39.350
I wonder what I should make today?

14:39.940 --> 14:41.770
So you're all right now, huh?

14:42.110 --> 14:45.320
I guess I'd be lying if I said I wasn't lonely, but yeah.

14:45.320 --> 14:47.190
Hiro-kun was aiming for that job.

14:47.190 --> 14:49.240
I have to cheer him on, you know?

14:49.240 --> 14:51.410
You've become stronger, haven't you?

14:51.410 --> 14:54.280
Once you have a place to return to, you become stronger.

14:55.080 --> 14:56.700
When I didn't have anything,

14:56.700 --> 15:00.710
I used to think that I'd be stronger if I had nothing to lose.

15:02.170 --> 15:05.000
I guess I don't have a use for this anymore.

15:05.000 --> 15:07.010
me

15:15.970 --> 15:17.850
Akane, is <i>this what you want?</i>

15:17.850 --> 15:20.270
Nah, I'm just looking at it.

15:26.900 --> 15:28.030
Akane?

15:28.030 --> 15:30.110
I get cold if I'm by myself.

15:31.950 --> 15:33.570
At least take it off when you're sleeping.

15:33.570 --> 15:34.530
I don't want to.

15:34.530 --> 15:36.080
You like it <i>that much?</i>

15:36.080 --> 15:36.990
Yeah.

15:36.990 --> 15:40.750
Onii-chan, you actually wanted to buy paint, didn't you?

15:40.750 --> 15:41.460
Nope.

15:41.460 --> 15:42.580
Liar.

15:42.580 --> 15:44.290
I'm not lying!

15:44.290 --> 15:46.750
Thanks. I'll treasure it, okay?

15:46.750 --> 15:48.050
Yeah.

15:48.050 --> 15:49.420
Good night.

15:49.420 --> 15:50.630
Good night.

15:57.310 --> 15:58.180
An earthquake?!

15:58.180 --> 15:59.060
Akane? Where are you?!

15:59.060 --> 15:59.560
Akane?!

16:00.730 --> 16:01.940
Onii-chan?

16:02.190 --> 16:03.190
Akane!

16:10.490 --> 16:12.240
Onii-chan! Onii-chan!

16:12.860 --> 16:14.110
Akane!

16:14.740 --> 16:16.780
Onii-chan, where are you?!

16:16.780 --> 16:20.250
Onii-chan, where did you go?!

16:28.550 --> 16:30.550
Fingertips

16:30.550 --> 16:32.090
Sorry about today.

16:32.090 --> 16:33.180
Nah.

16:33.180 --> 16:34.220
Do you wanna drink a little?

16:34.220 --> 16:35.220
I'll pass.

16:35.220 --> 16:37.390
Come on, relax at my house once in a while.

16:37.390 --> 16:39.100
Chihiro-chan's waiting for you, isn't she?

16:39.600 --> 16:41.180
I guess you're right.

16:42.930 --> 16:43.980
Do you need something?

16:44.730 --> 16:46.440
Could you go buy me a calendar?

16:46.730 --> 16:47.690
A calendar?

16:48.320 --> 16:49.610
Hey, Kuze...

16:49.610 --> 16:51.190
Hmm?

16:51.190 --> 16:52.820
Aren't you scared?

16:52.820 --> 16:55.530
Man, why are you asking this <i>now?</i>

16:55.530 --> 16:57.200
I'm asking this because it <i>is now.</i>

16:59.410 --> 17:01.620
Of course I'm scared.

17:02.540 --> 17:04.620
Don't say things like that with a laugh

17:20.060 --> 17:23.020
I'm sorry about being in bed all day yesterday.

17:23.020 --> 17:25.270
No, I should be the one to apologize.

17:25.270 --> 17:27.560
Basically, it's my fault you got sick.

17:27.560 --> 17:29.560
What were you doing yesterday?

17:29.560 --> 17:31.860
I was thinking about you all day long.

17:31.860 --> 17:35.240
Geez, y-you say embarrassing things without a thought, don't you?

17:35.240 --> 17:38.280
Well, there isn't really anything else I want to think about at the moment.

17:38.280 --> 17:39.370
Could you wait a second?

17:39.740 --> 17:41.870
I'm going to take this in for repairs.

17:45.710 --> 17:48.710
When we're like this, I feel like a winner as a woman.

17:49.080 --> 17:52.550
When you view this as an outsider, it kinda pisses you off, doesn't it?

17:53.170 --> 17:55.840
You're not romantic at all, even though you're a musician.

17:55.840 --> 17:57.800
That's because I've retired from being a musician.

17:57.800 --> 18:01.850
Well then, can't you pretend to be my lover like a normal person would?

18:01.850 --> 18:03.140
But I'm not your lover.

18:04.310 --> 18:07.600
Can't we become lovers?

18:07.600 --> 18:11.560
Mizuki-chan, the fact that I'm going to die is not a joke.

18:11.560 --> 18:12.860
I know that.

18:13.070 --> 18:16.400
I can only do things like this for so long.

18:16.400 --> 18:18.240
Are you going to be hospitalized?

18:18.530 --> 18:19.660
Eventually.

18:19.660 --> 18:21.990
That's why I'm clearing the decks before that time comes.

18:21.990 --> 18:23.450
Clearing the decks?

18:23.450 --> 18:26.410
Well, first I sorted out all my interpersonal relationships.

18:26.410 --> 18:29.670
Then to get ready for death, I disposed of all my possessions, other than documents.

18:30.290 --> 18:32.670
That violin was the last of them.

18:33.000 --> 18:35.670
Is it okay if I ask something that may seem unnecessary?

18:35.670 --> 18:36.420
Go ahead.

18:36.970 --> 18:40.220
Kuze-san, were you perhaps dating someone?

18:40.220 --> 18:41.140
I was.

18:42.260 --> 18:43.600
I loved her.

18:43.600 --> 18:45.850
We loved each other, and we were even engaged.

18:48.350 --> 18:50.020
That's why I broke up with her.

18:48.350 --> 18:50.480
That's why... we broke up

18:54.110 --> 18:55.530
I'm sorry.

18:56.480 --> 18:59.030
Ah, a sunshower.

19:05.160 --> 19:06.580
Hey, Miya-chan.

19:06.580 --> 19:08.000
Here's dinner.

19:08.000 --> 19:09.160
Where's Hiro-kun?

19:09.160 --> 19:12.040
He collapsed right after he finished his manuscript a little while ago.

19:12.040 --> 19:14.250
Well then, please make him eat this when he wakes up.

19:14.250 --> 19:15.630
There's some for you too, Nagi-san.

19:15.630 --> 19:16.880
Thanks.

19:16.880 --> 19:18.880
Are you sure you don't want to eat with us?

19:18.880 --> 19:20.680
No, please let him sleep.

19:20.680 --> 19:23.510
I'll make him repay me for this for the rest of his life.

19:23.510 --> 19:24.640
Gotcha.

19:24.640 --> 19:27.180
When he wakes up, I'll punch him for you.

19:27.180 --> 19:28.680
Yup!

19:35.900 --> 19:37.280
This is a surprise.

19:37.280 --> 19:40.530
This is the first time I've ever seen him <i>this carefree.</i>

19:40.530 --> 19:42.030
Himura-san!

19:42.030 --> 19:43.950
Did you hear about his disease?

19:43.950 --> 19:45.280
Yes.

19:45.280 --> 19:48.160
If you keep on going this way, you'll have a terrible experience.

19:48.160 --> 19:49.540
You're probably right,

19:49.540 --> 19:50.790
but I'll manage.

19:51.120 --> 19:56.040
Only humans are able to record the day they'll die on their calendar.

19:56.040 --> 20:01.010
Perhaps he feels it's better than an unexpected end, or perhaps it's just a bad joke.

20:01.010 --> 20:05.050
How can you stay calm like that, Himura-san?

20:05.050 --> 20:08.390
I'm used to others dying. Just a little bit.

20:08.390 --> 20:10.520
Was it... the earthquake?

20:12.020 --> 20:14.560
Are you unafraid because you're used to it?

20:14.560 --> 20:15.520
It's the exact opposite.

20:15.520 --> 20:17.270
I'm terrified.

20:17.650 --> 20:21.820
Because I know the pain, I feel as though I'd be crushed if I didn't continue to smile.

20:21.820 --> 20:26.870
But I've watched the people and the city that arose from it.

20:26.870 --> 20:30.790
It looks like I put you through something that turned out better than I expected.

20:30.790 --> 20:31.750
I apologize.

20:31.750 --> 20:34.250
No, thanks a lot.

20:34.250 --> 20:37.250
If you change your mind, feel free to come punch me.

20:37.250 --> 20:39.090
Umm, Himura-san!

20:39.090 --> 20:39.800
What is it?

20:39.800 --> 20:42.050
Could you please say that thing?

20:42.050 --> 20:44.630
The thing that goes, "May God's aid be with us".

20:45.590 --> 20:47.800
I'm neither a priest nor a pastor.

20:47.800 --> 20:50.060
But it still suits you.

20:50.430 --> 20:52.560
"May the Force be with you."

20:52.560 --> 20:54.140
What's that?

20:54.600 --> 20:57.150
It's a lot more decent than God is.

20:59.480 --> 21:01.110
Mizuki-chan?

21:01.110 --> 21:02.490
Mizuki-chan.

21:04.400 --> 21:05.410
Did you wake up?

21:05.410 --> 21:08.120
Oh... when did I doze off?

21:08.120 --> 21:10.700
Were there any more sunshowers?

21:10.700 --> 21:11.410
Huh?

21:11.410 --> 21:15.460
Because if there were, I might've been drooling this time.

21:15.460 --> 21:17.420
I'll just pretend I didn't notice.

21:21.170 --> 21:25.380
Mizuki-chan, what do you want to be in the future?

21:25.380 --> 21:27.140
I haven't decided yet.

21:27.140 --> 21:28.140
But...

21:28.140 --> 21:30.810
I guess I want to be happy!

21:30.810 --> 21:31.760
I see.

21:31.760 --> 21:34.020
Well, I like you too.

21:35.980 --> 21:40.360
That's why I can't reciprocate your feelings.

21:40.360 --> 21:41.730
Go home now.

21:41.730 --> 21:42.780
And...

21:42.780 --> 21:46.030
please don't ever come see me again.

22:01.420 --> 22:14.810
The shining wind calmly sways from gaps in the clouds.

22:15.390 --> 22:22.230
The echoing sounds sparkle.

22:22.360 --> 22:25.740
Even if it's a hope that was nearly lost,

22:25.990 --> 22:33.370
I should be able to find it again

22:35.660 --> 22:38.540
Holding firmly onto your sound,

22:39.170 --> 22:48.720
I don't let go of your hand joined with mine.

22:49.680 --> 22:55.520
Please don't forget the important things.

22:56.680 --> 23:03.190
A smile continues on into the future.

23:23.540 --> 23:25.000
<i>Fine.</i>

23:25.840 --> 23:27.840
Words of atonement,

23:27.840 --> 23:30.130
and the intertwined hearts.

23:30.130 --> 23:33.140
ef - a tale of melodies.

23:33.140 --> 23:35.430
Utter.

23:35.430 --> 23:38.470
Can you hear it? The melody of truth.
